WEBVTT

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.920
You're heading to the lab now, right? Hop in.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.010
No, but...

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.550
Just get in.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.100
The inside of this car is my kingdom.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.440
Even the power of Melchizedek, which rules over
every corner of this management district...

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.780
...doesn't reach here. That's the contract.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:32.950
Contract...

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.620
A special contract comes with a heavy price.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.910
This is a tiny kingdom, but someday...

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.500
...I'll expand out to the entire city.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.750
You really are amazing, Lord Kyohma.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.920
Just call me Kyohma.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.970
The circumstances were a bit unusual,
but you became a warrior as well.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.510
But...

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.260
I won't let you watch my back
until I know how you think.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.690
So let's hear what you're really after.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.800
Sortie: Noble and Fleeting

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.740
Yes. What you're really after.

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.450
Why did you decide to join the battle?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.450
Don't say it's to "save this world."

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.080
It can't possibly be something that shallow.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.250
It's not to protect Kyoka, either.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.720
According to the reports I received,
you opened the case slightly earlier than she did.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.090
Then Kyoka also...

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.600
Yeah. You didn't hear?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.430
So what about you?

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.230
You have a different reason, right?

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.770
Something you haven't mentioned at the lab yet.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.480
For instance...

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:18.190
The fact that you warped to Japan of 2015 by yourself.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.990
Does it have something to do with that?

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.410
Bullseye?

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.870
You might not believe this, but...

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.040
A kid asked you for help, huh?

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.340
You mean her, right?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.800
You were watching?

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:42.180
Kyoka doesn't know,
but I assigned bodyguards to her.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.970
The Katagiri family has many enemies.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.020
I myself have several,
as does my little sister.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.270
If something unusual happens around her,
I immediately get a report.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.360
Hey.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.690
Don't ever tell her this.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.950
She'd hate me.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.450
Don't laugh. I'm serious!

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:06.580
I'm sorry.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.330
But still, I never realized there were bodyguards.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.710
They're hiding. Just like this!

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.050
It was a huge success, right Lord Kyohma?

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.210
Wh-Where have you been until now...

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.470
Humans have more blind spots
than they realize.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.430
Don't underestimate Sidune.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.220
She may not look it, but she's the most veteran of them all.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:32.640
The Rindo family has served
the Katagiri family for generations,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.320
as bodyguards, spies, and assassins.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.750
You know how to get
to the training facility, right?

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.540
You're heading straight there today.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.290
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.380
I'll join up later.
So go get your butt kicked.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.510
Got it.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.050
It doesn't look like
he's fully committed to doing this.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.970
He can't help it.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.850
People like you are very special, Lord Kyohma.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.690
We should get going, too.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.600
Yes, my master!

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.320
My uniform?

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.360
It's a bit different...

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:28.990
<i>That combat suit comes with
a G-Splitter already embedded in it.</i>

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.580
<i>You read the manual, right?</i>

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.580
It's a miniature inertial control system, right?

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:36.330
<i>Correct.</i>

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.420
<i>It allows high-speed movement
by controlling gravity.</i>

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:45.340
<i>It also functions as a defensive field that lessens physical impacts.</i>

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.430
Where does it get its power?

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.930
<i>CP energy is fed to it
from a weapon affected by the Cube.</i>

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.730
<i>Now, please put it on.</i>

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.070
Um, how long are you going to be watching?

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:12.040
<i>I'm checking your physical condition.
Is that a problem?</i>

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.910
Don't tease me!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.830
<i>I'll have someone come pick you up.</i>

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.580
<i>So when you're ready,
please exit the room.</i>

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:24.960
This is a ghost.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.510
A ghost?

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.680
A fuzzy image of a human sometimes seen on the battlefield.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:36.560
I've encountered one before,
and they've shown up in other people's reports too.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.270
I think it was Brian
that decided to call them ghosts.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.780
But this is the first time I've seen one that's so clear.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.360
When it happened, I'd been chasing after her...

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.240
...and I fell from some place that looked like a factory.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.950
It showed up inside
the management district too, huh?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.710
That's a big deal, yeah.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:03.380
And so you decided to join the battle
to check this thing out.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.010
Another factor,
distinct from the Timekeepers...

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:11.220
Ghost-hunting doesn't sound that appealing to me.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.560
What's wrong?
You look like you've seen a ghost.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.860
Or maybe a dead man?

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.410
Um, who are you?

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.780
Grab it. Real flesh and bone.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.120
I'm Aaron Burroughs.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.830
I've joined the operation as a mercenary.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:46.550
What you saw was the me in the other universe...
the enemy's Aaron Burroughs.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.010
I took him down.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:54.510
You're going to join the training program here.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:58.390
We can't just dump you on the battlefield without training.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.390
That is, until we hear something
from the Timekeepers?

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:05.190
That's right. Their messages always appear without warning.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:09.940
I don't know how many days we have,
but I'd like you to learn the basics of team battle.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:14.280
But in any case,
you're Tohru Kazasumi.

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:17.240
To be honest, I have high expectations of you.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.700
Is he that strong?

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.960
Yes. A formidable opponent.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:26.710
Um, there's something I'd like to ask...

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.750
What is it?

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:34.010
How did feel... to fight yourself... and kill yourself?

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:37.470
I may be a mercenary, but I'm still a soldier.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.770
It's my job to fight on the battlefield and win.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.730
If needed, I can kill anyone...

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.690
...and I'm prepared to die on the battlefield at any time.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.650
Is that how it works?

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.490
It's not a great feeling.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.410
Let's go! I'm not gonna hold back!

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:02.460
You missed!

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.130
Come on, let's go!

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.840
W-Wait, time out!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.470
Nope, not letting you get away!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.850
Wrong place!

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.810
I'm going to play a little trick.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.980
Go!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:41.160
Look, look, Tohru!
My own personal combat suit!

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.750
Y-Yeah...

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:45.620
We match!

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:48.210
<i>Kyoka Katagiri has left the field.</i>

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:50.380
<i>The winner is Remy Odhner.</i>

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:52.090
Oh, drat.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:55.010
Don't turn your back on 
the enemy during a fight.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.590
If you did that on the battlefield,
you'd be blown apart.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.470
Yes sir, instructor!

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.480
That worked up a good sweat!

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:18.320
I'm sorry, Remy.
Let's spar again sometime, okay?

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.620
F-Fine.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.250
You made up your mind.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:29.170
Yeah.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:33.960
I decided to fight as well.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:52.860
Yes. Right now, we're practicing a situation where multiple battles are going on in the same area.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:57.030
Yes. It's only day three, but they've made
 remarkable progress, haven't they?

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.530
You fell for it!

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.920
Dammit, how many of those can you throw?

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.970
You underestimated me, didn't you?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.720
I didn't think I was!

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.730
I told you, didn't I?

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.110
You have to watch your blind spots.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.190
I give up...

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.400
You can totally tell you're an amateur.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.530
If you went to a battle like that...

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:47.080
I'm training for the sake of Lord Kyohma.
I can't lose that easily!

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:55.750
<i>Again!?</i>

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.020
What the hell was that?

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.810
<i>That's your ability.</i>

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.820
<i>Nth dimensional space-orientation function.</i>

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:20.700
<i>The ability to understand spatial relations
and control your location within the flow of time.</i>

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.200
Nth dimensional?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:27.240
Well, we just use an acronym and call it NDSF.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:31.620
<i>In the brains of eligible people,
this function is very active.</i>

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:35.130
It was an accident. Sorry about that.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:38.090
I'll just leave it at that.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.960
There won't be a second time, though.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.720
Is something the matter?

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:47.560
Lord Remy.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.600
It's nothing much.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.060
<i>A psychic created by human experimentation...</i>

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:59.190
<i>I guess I'm not that different, though.</i>

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:02.400
How is the training going?

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:07.080
They're very quick to catch on.
They were able to use the gravity control in no time.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:11.500
It seems like they've done their share
of the combat curriculum at the academy as well.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.170
Arcturus Academy, huh?

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:20.380
We used that place, as it was part of the Melchizedek group,
in an effort to gather the eligible close to the lab.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:24.550
Your idea paid off in an unexpected way, though.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:28.890
That academy is where the future leaders of Melchizedek are born.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.060
They need to at least be able to defend themselves.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:33.940
And so you're sure this is all right?

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:38.480
I'll keep a close eye on Lady Kyoka.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.900
Yeah, please do.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.860
So Lord Kyohma,
please do the job you need to do.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.530
She chose for herself.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.660
I have no right to stop that.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.830
<i>Emergency. Emergency.</i>

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:59.750
<i>All operations personnel
immediately report to the briefing room.</i>

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:04.090
<i>Repeat. Immediately report to the briefing room.</i>

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.380
What's this?

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.260
Looks like they're here.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:08.350
Yeah.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.060
It's the Timekeepers.

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:17.440
Operation system, commence phase two.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.610
<i>Nothing unusual on the bio-scans.</i>

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.610
Target Group NDSF detected.
Commencing brain-wave tracking.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:28.320
Anti-tachyon circuits booted.
Commencing weak boson propagation

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.200
Circuit has reached criticality.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.870
Chrono potential at 95% of theoretical values.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.170
Creation of CP field confirmed.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.340
This is the final checkup.
We have no time, so I'll keep this brief.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:46.170
We'll be warped into the Shibuya area,
but we don't know where we'll end up.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:50.220
We'll be squad A, and old man
Aaron will lead in squad B after us,

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:52.560
but the chance of us
landing in the same location is low.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.560
How effective are the defensive fields?

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:57.520
They can withstand
a certain amount of attacks,

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.900
but I don't know what happens when the
 enemy weapon's firepower overwhelms us...

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.980
Avoid direct hits as much as possible.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.650
As much as possible?

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:09.530
If you're heavily injured,
the operator can initiate a forced return.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:15.700
But if you're dead, there's nothing we can do. That's when it's "game over."

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:20.790
<i>Final confirmation complete.
Time vault 03, release!</i>

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:27.380
Kyoka, this is your first battle.
Don't pull ahead of the group.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.930
Why are you acting so high and mighty,
stupid big brother?

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.100
Who are you calling stupid?

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.260
Leave me alone!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.180
Don't do that so suddenly!

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.230
Your G-Splitter, idiot!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:45.690
Be careful!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:46.690
Sorry!

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.360
Look. Over there!

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:53.830
So they really do exist...

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.960
Okay, I'll...

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.500
...knock them even further out of position.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:05.880
You never give me a break, do you?

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:07.710
So this is the match up, huh?

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.130
It doesn't matter who I'm fighting,
I do the same thing.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.220
Let's go, guys!

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:18.520
Everyone, stay close!
They're trying to pick you off one by one!

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:21.140
I know that! I know that, but...

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:35.830
Tohru!

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.290
Don't come here! They'll snipe you!

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.750
He's got cold feet.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.540
It's understandable...

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.880
Maybe bringing two people with no experience on the same mission wasn't a good idea...

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.010
Sidune, about my little sister...

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:52.010
<i>Leave her to me!</i>

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:57.930
I'll play with you right now!

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.640
Eat this!

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.190
At that rate he's eventually going to run out of bullets.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.150
I'm here, too!

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.480
So she finally came over, huh?

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:09.480
Wow, they really do look like us...

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:14.910
<i>Lady Kyoka, you shouldn't overextend your position!</i>

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:16.700
You can't get away!

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:20.040
I told you not to do that!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:23.580
Listen to what others tell you, you tomboy!

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:25.330
Who did you call a tomboy?

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:35.510
I failed to eliminate them.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:45.480
<i>Kyohma!</i>

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.860
What? I'm kinda busy!

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.070
<i>That girl may be nearby!</i>

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.070
The ghost?

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.030
<i>I don't know, but...</i>

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:58.160
Are you all right?

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.870
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.870
Change of plans!

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.660
Sidune, Kyoka, rendezvous with me!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.960
<i>Roger that. Come on, Lady Kyoka!</i>

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:09.920
<i>Wait a minute!</i>

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.340
<i>Kyohma, I...</i>

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:14.220
I'll give you two and a half minutes.
Capture that ghost.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:16.260
Ghost?

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.470
I'll explain later!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.930
<i>Two and a half minutes.
Remember that!</i>

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.260
Got it!

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.850
Yes, I'll be visiting your company right now...

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:29.480
What's the meaning of this, Big Brother?

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:31.940
I asked him to search the area.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.740
Hey, explain. What's this about a ghost?

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:36.650
It's the girl you saw before.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.790
At any rate, right now...

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.580
...he won't be much help in battle.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.290
We're going to change our formation!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:53.800
Perfect. There's someone
worth taking out our aggression on.

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:59.550
You think you can fight without Tohru Kazasumi...
It looks like you underestimate me.

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:03.560
They look just like each other, too.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:22.740
Be careful.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.710
Time... will end...

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:27.750
Wait!

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.330
The future hasn't been determined yet.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.630
So that's a ghost?

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:36.550
Remy...

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:40.510
Those crows were a terminal for the Timekeepers.

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.890
You'll see them often in the management district, too.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.350
Do you know something?

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:48.980
I heard that the Timekeepers
are all from the future.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:53.900
Since they have more advanced technology than we do, it's probably true.

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.570
From the future, huh?

00:19:55.570 --> 00:20:00.410
The ghosts are probably also from the future, and they're their enemies.

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:03.240
Anyway, that's what Kyohma says.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.950
"The future hasn't been determined yet."

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.960
Maybe that's why they're so fuzzy.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.870
You heard?

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:15.380
I usually can't hear.
It must be because you're next to me.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:20.630
But having you leave the battle and decreasing our firepower?

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.840
What the hell is Kyohma thinking?

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:24.050
But you...

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:27.600
I'm scouting. Don't compare me to you.

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:31.600
I'm sorry! I need to get back!

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:34.690
Wait! I need information from you, too!

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:38.440
<i>Squad A has entered combat.
Some have been injured!</i>

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.780
Lord Kyohma's field...

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:48.120
They separated us?

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.410
Where the hell is their Tohru?

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.120
Big Brother!

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:57.670
Don't get in my way!

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.190
Kyohma! Behind you!

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.810
Sidune?

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.780
We got a fan letter!

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:29.990
"Who's stronger, Dogma or Magma?" It says.

00:23:29.990 --> 00:23:33.030
We're a team, but we're also rivals!
A battle is inevitable!

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:35.040
Going down together,
the two corpses side by side...

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.620
The battle continues to the ends of hell!

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.920
<b><i>Confrontation </i></b>Those Who Defend time<i><b></b></i>

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:38.940
Next episode: "Confrontation"

00:23:38.940 --> 00:23:39.920
"Those Who Defend Time"
